REGENT OF KARIMUN
Considering : a. that all forms of Violence Against Women and Children constitute violations of human rights, therefore the Regional Government is obligated to provide Protection and fulfillment of the rights of women and Children from all forms of Violence;
b. that the implementation of Protection of women and Children in Karimun Regency has not been carried out optimally and comprehensively, therefore efforts to improve the Protection of women and Children need to be undertaken;
c. that to provide direction, foundation and legal certainty to all parties involved in the implementation of Protection of women and Children, a regulation is required;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 53 of 1999 concerning the Establishment of Pelalawan Regency, Rokan Hulu Regency, Rokan Hilir Regency, Siak Regency, Karimun Regency, Natuna Regency, Kuantan Singingi Regency and Batam City (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 181, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3902) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 34 of 2008 concerning the Third Amendment to Law Number 53 of 1999 concerning the Establishment of Pelalawan Regency, Rokan Hulu Regency, Rokan Hilir Regency, Siak Regency, Karimun Regency, Natuna Regency, Kuantan Singingi Regency and Batam City (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 107, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4880);
